# Navigation links

Any UI that navigates to an in-app route must render a real anchor via React Router `Link` (or `NavMenuLink` in `components/navigation/NavMenuLink.tsx`).

Do **not** use `<button onClick={() => navigate(...)}>` for menu items, sidebar entries, or dashboard quick links.

- Enables right-click → Open in new tab, middle-click, and copy link address.
- Reserve `<button>` for actions that do not change the URL (toggle, logout, submit).
